Z||000000||batt||10-14-2001||04:51 PM||||im sure fieros are great cars, but im 15 and i am soon to be needing a car. are fieros god for the job? i heard that they are hard to fix due to no engine space, but do they break often? if fieros do not make good 1st cars what would be a good *fun* to drive car for a 1st timer?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Posthumane||10-14-2001||05:04 PM||||It is my first and serves great. It actually has quite a bit of room in the engine bay, but the location makes it hard to get at. But that doesn't really bother me, you just need to learn to get into wierd places.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pilrulz||10-14-2001||05:08 PM||||fieros do make good first cars.  i'll be 15 next month, and i'm so far pleased with mine.  don't know where you heard that there's no engine space, cause i think there's a lot of room in there. <P>                       pil ||||reg||12
Z||000003||85ZainoGT||10-14-2001||05:30 PM||||well I will be 17 in less than a month, and my 85gt was/is my first car, and I love it, although I am looking to buy another fiero, you want to buy mine.. $2200, no problems yet this far!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
