Z||000014||GTFiero1||10-14-2001||07:55 PM||||im going for a v-6 when i get my first fiero. 4 bangers have way to little power to stisfy me. 140hp isn't even enough. more the better. i wanna blow away anyone who makes fun of my car<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Kasdan||10-14-2001||09:36 PM||||I think the 60* V6 is a great engine to have in a first car.  Ive had it in both my first cars, my first was a 90 Lumina Euro Coupe, that was a great car, i just wish i had kept it a little longer to put that 180 HP 3.1 in it(the fiero) that i worked so hard on.  My second, you guessed it, is my 86 GT.  I am currently 16 (17 NEXT MONTH!)<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">           <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroKyle||10-14-2001||09:44 PM||||Its an alright first car, my 85GT is my first, I am 16. The only thing is me being the age I am, every dollar I make goes into insurance and keeping it runnin though. I have also have purchased a winter beater because I really do not want to drive it in the winter because of its condition and its history of never been drove in the winter. Just me 2 cents though. I don't reccomend the car if ya have money issues.||||reg||1
